{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cet8mYSVXWjTj67hV8tY2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All existing tests pass (13 tests). Now I have a complete picture of the repository. Let me summarize the findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model with status enum at: `Shipment.kt:23-26`\n- ShipmentController has create/get/list at: `ShipmentController.kt:26-56`\n- Repository provides save/findById/existsById at: `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-26`\n- Error handling via ApiExceptions.kt (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException)\n- ErrorCode enum at: `ApiError.kt:31-37` (currently ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED)\n\n**Conventions found:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses, never build error bodies themselves\n2. ErrorCode is a closed enum used for all errors (part of public API)\n3. No service layer—logic is directly in controllers\n4. Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions on response bodies\n5. Tests verify error envelope's `error.code` field\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n2. `ApiError.kt` — must add new ErrorCode for shipment state conflict\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add comprehensive tests\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding ErrorCode is part of public API contract\n- Idempotency: repeated confirm of CONFIRMED shipment must succeed without error\n- State transitions: CANCELLED → confirm must fail with 409\n\n**Open questions:** None—ticket is clear and patterns are established.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED` error code to the ErrorCode enum. This is specific, follows the pattern of existing codes, and clearly documents why the operation failed.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add method:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment\n   ```\n   Logic: \n   - Find shipment by ID or throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED)\n   - If status is CREATED, update to CONFIRMED, save, return\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return unchanged (idempotent)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four test methods:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment and persists it` — POST confirm, GET to verify status changed\n   - `confirm is idempotent for CONFIRMED shipments` — confirm twice, verify second call succeeds with same body\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with proper error code` — create with CANCELLED in repo, confirm fails with 409 and error.code\n   - `reports unknown shipment on confirm` — confirm non-existent shipment returns 404\n\n**Alternative rejected:** I considered not adding a new ErrorCode and reusing VALIDATION_FAILED, but that would be inconsistent with existing patterns where each specific failure has its own code. The ticket emphasizes \"consistent with the rest of this API,\" which means each case should have a specific, stable error code.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | findById(id) | save(shipment.copy(status=CONFIRMED)) | Shipment | 200 OK |\n| CONFIRMED → retry | findById(id) | save(shipment.copy(status=CONFIRMED)) | Shipment | 200 OK (idempotent) |\n| CANCELLED | findById(id) | (none) | error envelope | 409 ConflictException |\n| Not found | findById(id) | (none) | error envelope | 404 ResourceNotFoundException |\n\nAll flows go through repository.findById() or throw exceptions caught by GlobalExceptionHandler.\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Confirm CREATED**: Assert response body contains status=CONFIRMED, then GET the shipment to verify persistence through a second request (per testing-and-verification skill).\n2. **Idempotent CONFIRMED**: Create, confirm once, confirm again, assert second response body matches first (per skill: repeat exercise).\n3. **Reject CANCELLED**: Insert CANCELLED shipment directly in repository (fixture setup), attempt confirm, assert 409 with error.code=SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM_CANCELLED, GET to verify state unchanged.\n4. **Unknown shipment**: Confirm non-existent ID, assert 404 with error.code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND.\n\nEach test follows the skill's four requirements: body assertion, separate GET, re-assertion after refusal, and error code verification.\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nI'll now implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2466,"cache_read_input_tokens":22502,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2466},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1058045f-cd1f-4bb8-be49-590a14251379","uuid":"00b84f79-090e-4783-adef-8b8edb519e27","timestamp":"2026-09-09T15:53:26.785Z","request_id":"req_011Cet8mXSDnSP6Fr4mnoFBb"}
